    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I've added the following code to my `after/ftplugin/tex.lua` file:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal mp = require(\"mini.pairs\")\r\nmp.map_buf(0, \"i\", \"$\", { action = \"closeopen\", pair = \"$$\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works perfectly for adding the second $ when I enter math mode in LaTeX by typing the first $. But, any brackets entered inside  the pair don't add the second one, unless there's a space.\r\n\r\nInstead of ending up with (where | is the cursor)\r\n```\r\nThis is an equation: $f(|)$\r\n```\r\nI get\r\n```\r\nThis is an equation: $f(|$\r\n```\r\n\r\nHow can I get that round bracket to close automatically? It works if I enter a space after the opening $ and before the closing $, but not otherwise. Am I setting it up wrong, or is there something I need to add?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I've added the following code to my <code class=\"notranslate\">after/ftplugin/tex.lua</code> file:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local mp = require(&quot;mini.pairs&quot;)\nmp.map_buf(0, &quot;i&quot;, &quot;$&quot;, { action = &quot;closeopen&quot;, pair = &quot;$$&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">mp</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pairs<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">mp</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_buf</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>$<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>closeopen<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">pair</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>$$<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This works perfectly for adding the second $ when I enter math mode in LaTeX by typing the first $. But, any brackets entered inside  the pair don't add the second one, unless there's a space.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Instead of ending up with (where | is the cursor)</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"This is an equation: $f(|)$\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">This is an equation: $f(|)$\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I get</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"This is an equation: $f(|$\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">This is an equation: $f(|$\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How can I get that round bracket to close automatically? It works if I enter a space after the opening $ and before the closing $, but not otherwise. Am I setting it up wrong, or is there something I need to add?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I've added the following code to my after/ftplugin/tex.lua file:\nlocal mp = require(\"mini.pairs\")\nmp.map_buf(0, \"i\", \"$\", { action = \"closeopen\", pair = \"$$\" })\nThis works perfectly for adding the second $ when I enter math mode in LaTeX by typing the first $. But, any brackets entered inside  the pair don't add the second one, unless there's a space.\nInstead of ending up with (where | is the cursor)\nThis is an equation: $f(|)$\n\nI get\nThis is an equation: $f(|$\n\nHow can I get that round bracket to close automatically? It works if I enter a space after the opening $ and before the closing $, but not otherwise. Am I setting it up wrong, or is there something I need to add?",
