                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Sorry for spamming, just doing multiple tests. It seems this happens for me with any `closeopen` pair, in any file type.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why this would happen, but suppose I'm in a lua file, and I enter a `\"` to open a string. The closing `\"` appears, but then if I type a `(` or a `[`, the closing `)` or `]` won't appear.\r\n\r\nThis happened for me with `\"` and `'`, in lua, Python, and a basic text file.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry for spamming, just doing multiple tests. It seems this happens for me with any <code class=\"notranslate\">closeopen</code> pair, in any file type.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not sure why this would happen, but suppose I'm in a lua file, and I enter a <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> to open a string. The closing <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> appears, but then if I type a <code class=\"notranslate\">(</code> or a <code class=\"notranslate\">[</code>, the closing <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">]</code> won't appear.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This happened for me with <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code>, in lua, Python, and a basic text file.</p>",
